L432: Acknowledgments
L433: The authors would like to express their gratitude to Mariel Chagollan, Celia Guerrero, B.S. Anay Valencia, and B.S. Luis Gamez for their invaluable contributions to the completion of this article. Additionally, the authors would like to thank the Instituto de Investigación en Odontología-CUCS for providing the necessary facilities to carry out this research.
L434: **Supplementary Material**
L435: Flow cytometry apoptosis assay using Annexin V and PI staining to assess cellular apoptosis levels
L436: **Figure S1** . Antioxidant supplementation with GSH + NAC and ALL does not induce apoptosis
L437: in neutrophils. Freshly isolated neutrophils were supplemented with and without the
L438: antioxidant combinations GSH + NAC and ALL and incubated for 60 minutes. Apoptosis was
L439: assessed by flow cytometry using annexin V (BL1-A) and propidium iodide (BL2-A). a, b, and
L440: c) Representative dot-plot analysis for apoptosis assessment in neutrophils. The Q1 and Q2
L441: represent the dead cells, the Q3 the apoptotic cells and the Q4 the live cells. d) Percentage of
L442: live neutrophils with and without antioxidant supplementation. e) Percentage of apoptotic
L443: neutrophils with and without antioxidant supplementation. f) Percentage of dead neutrophils.
L444: A total of 20,000 events were acquired, and the sample size consisted of 4 subjects analyzed in
L445: duplicates. Statistical analysis was performed using the Friedman test. Results are presented
L446: as mean ± standard deviation SD.
L447: Cytotoxicity assay using the MTT Cell proliferation kit
L448: **Figure S2** . Antioxidant supplementation with GSH + NAC and ALL does not induce
L449: cytotoxicity in neutrophils. Freshly isolated neutrophils were supplemented with and without
L450: the antioxidant combinations GSH + NAC and ALL and incubated for 60 minutes. Cytotoxicity
L451: was assessed by measuring the conversion of water-soluble MTT into insoluble formazan by
L452: viable cells. The formazan crystals were subsequently solubilized with DMSO, generating a
L453: colored solution whose intensity is proportional to the concentration. The absorbance of the
L454: negative control and treated neutrophils showed no statistically significant difference. The
L455: sample size consisted of 4 subjects, and independent experiments were analyzed in triplicates.
L456: Statistical analysis was performed using one-way ANOVA followed by T3 Dunnett post hoc
L457: test. The results are presented as mean ± standard error (SE).
L458: Total Antioxidant Capacity (TAC) assay of media used
L459: **a)**
L460: **b)**
L461: **Figure S3.** Total Antioxidant Capacity assay of supplemented and non-supplemented culture
L462: media. a) The TAC of the individual media components, namely RPMI 1640, AS 2%, and RPMI
L463: 1640 + AS 2%, was measured independently. b) The TAC of RPMI 1640 + AS 2% supplemented
L464: with two different antioxidant combinations, GSH + NAC and ALL, was determined. The
L465: experiment was performed with one triplicate of each condition. The antioxidants were added
L466: to the media according to the instructions provided in the corresponding section of the
L467: materials and methods. The results are reported as the mean ± standard error (SE) of millimoles
L468: (mM) of trolox equivalent antioxidant capacity (TEAC).
L469: ROS Kinetics assessment during NET formation
L470: **Figure S4.** ROS production in stimulated neutrophils during NET formation. To assess ROS
L471: production, freshly isolated neutrophils incubated with the DCFDA probe and monitored for
L472: 180 minutes each 2 minutes. All samples contain 1.5 X 10 [5] neutrophils per well in RPMI 1640
L473: sodium bicarbonate buffered media (pH 7.3) + 2 % AS. Positive control and antioxidant groups
L474: (GSH + NAC and ALL) were stimulated with LPS. The time 0 corresponds to the initial
L475: measurement after neutrophil isolation and incubation with the DCFDA probe. The sample
L476: size was 4 subjects for each triplicate. Statistical analysis was performed analyzing the area
L477: under the curve (AUC) and performing one-way ANOVA and T3-Dunnet post hoc test. Results
L478: are presented as mean ± S.E. of median fluorescence intensity (MFI). Significant p values: < 0.03
L479: (*), < 0.001 (***).
